# Pyodide 0.29.0, pyodide.asm.js: read and write a string stored above 2 GiB of
# the heap at its real address.
#
# Upstream fix: https://github.com/pyodide/pyodide/pull/6217 ("Fix Python->JS
# string corruption when strings are allocated at >2GB memory locations"),
# which makes the shifts in src/core/jsmemops.h unsigned. It is first released
# in Pyodide 314.0.0; 0.29.x does not carry it. The pairs below are that
# change at the four places of the 0.29.0 build that convert strings:
# _python2js_ucs2 and _python2js_ucs4 (Python to JavaScript) and
# js2python_string (JavaScript to Python). A signed shift turns an address at
# or above 2^31 into a negative index, so the text came back as NUL characters
# or failed to convert.
#
# Format: each "-" line is text that occurs exactly once in the file; the "+"
# line after it replaces it. tools/verify_gui_offline.py vendor-assets applies
# the pairs and checks the result against PYODIDE_PATCH.sha256 in
# gbdraw/_web_assets.py.

- String.fromCharCode(HEAPU16[(ptr>>1)+i>>>0])
+ String.fromCharCode(HEAPU16[(ptr>>>1)+i>>>0])

- String.fromCodePoint(HEAPU32[(ptr>>2)+i>>>0])
+ String.fromCodePoint(HEAPU32[(ptr>>>2)+i>>>0])

- HEAPU32[(i>>2)+s>>>0]=r[s]
+ HEAPU32[(i>>>2)+s>>>0]=r[s]

- HEAPU16[(i>>1)+s>>>0]=r[s]
+ HEAPU16[(i>>>1)+s>>>0]=r[s]
